    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full suite passes: **51 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS** \u2014 including the new `Cp37Tests`.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change adds a read-only, derived `telephoneDisplay` field to the Owner response while leaving `telephone` as raw E.164.\n\n**`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `telephoneDisplay` property (`readOnly: true`) to the `Owner` schema, alongside the other derived-on-read fields like `displayName` and `contactPreference`. This is what regenerates `OwnerDto` with the new getter/setter at build time.\n\n**`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a `@Mapping(target = \"telephoneDisplay\", expression = \"java(deriveTelephoneDisplay(owner))\")` on `toOwnerDto`, plus the `deriveTelephoneDisplay` helper. It splits the stored E.164 number into country code + national digits (matching the known calling codes `+61`/`+1`, defaulting to a 2-digit code otherwise), then emits `\"+<cc> <national grouped in threes>\"`, e.g. `+61412345678` \u2192 `+61 412 345 678`. It returns `null` when telephone is absent and passes non-E.164 values through unchanged.\n\nI followed the existing codebase conventions \u2014 this mirrors exactly how the other derived Owner fields (`locality`, `ageBand`, `checkDigit`) are declared in the OpenAPI spec and computed via default methods in the MapStruct mapper.",
